Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 13:13:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04675/11362] [outer-loop] PoE-World weighted
 product-of-experts: built + fairly-tested honest null (loses to max-vote)

Operator-directed ('PoE-World program-synthesis'). PoE-World (arXiv:2505.10819): a weighted
product-of-experts world model. The naive product (max-vote ProductWorldModel) already exists
and NULLED (exp4749), so per the Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline this builds the GENUINELY
DIFFERENT mechanism (weighted-consensus combination + held-out-fitted/pruned log-odds weights),
names exp4749, and gates retire_if_same on the consensus actually firing.

DELIVERED (module/test/agent-wiring landed via conductor sweeps; this commit banks harness+result):
- arc_poe_world_model.py: PoEWorldModel (per-cell WEIGHTED-CONSENSUS argmax, NOT highest-trust
  max-vote) + fit_poe_weights (log-odds from held-out accuracy; no-evidence experts keep a prior
  weight so a sparse pool does not collapse to identity) + harvest_color_rewrite_experts (broad
  OVERLAPPING experts so per-cell votes can CONFLICT) + per-cell conflict telemetry.
- arc_poe_world_model_ab.py: offline transition-prediction A/B (fast; no live search), same expert
  pool both arms, prior swept {0.0,0.5}, conflict-gated verdict.
- competition_agent.py: PoE candidate flag-gated OFF (CARNOT_ARC_POE_WORLD), live-path-reachable.
- 6 unit tests (assert the consensus-vs-maxvote differentiator); orphan lint 44 modules; ruff clean.

HONEST RESULT (results/arc_poe_world_model_ab.json, adversarial_verify clean): consensus EXERCISED
(8 conflict cells, exercised=True), prior swept (0.0 fairer, used). PoE best-prior cell_recall 0.178
vs max-vote 0.558 -> NO lift, PoE loses in 0/4 games. WHY: ARC transitions are governed by a SINGLE
rule per cell, so selecting the single most-accurate expert (max-vote) beats BLENDING conflicting
experts (consensus dilutes the best expert); PoE's pruning of val-inaccurate experts also hurts on a
small val split. Converges with the exp4749 null: the combination rule is not a win on ARC's per-cell
determinism. retire_if_same_verdict=True (legitimately -- consensus was tested).

Adversarial sub-agent review (GAPS_FOUND) drove three fixes now in place: (1) GAP-1 consensus-never-
fired -> added broad overlapping experts + conflict telemetry + exercised gate; (2) prior handicap ->
prior sweep; (3) premature-retire/over-claim -> retire gated on consensus_exercised + corrected
interpretation. n=4 games (small) disclosed.

